Z||000000||PocketRocket||10-18-2001||10:11 AM||||I have both a 85 Fiero GT 4 speed and a 97 Mustang V6 5 Speed (which is faster than blackmustang95's) and I know for a fact that my Fiero can easily keep up with my mustang.  I'm not trashing either because I love them both.  I just wanted to clear that up.<P>Fiero Mods:<BR>K&N<BR>Holly Side Scoop<BR>Superchip<BR>Straight Pipes<P>Mustang Mods:<BR>K&N<BR>Future: Air Intake & Exhuast<P> <IMG SRC="http://pages.prodigy.net/fourtrax200/larry04medium.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by PocketRocket (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||10-18-2001||10:28 AM||||I don't see this topic lasting too long  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">   Maybe if we all play really nice Cliff will let us play with this topic for a while... it can be a good one.  <P>I don't think comparisons between the two are exactly fair anyway.  A new Mustang vs a 14-18 year old Fiero?  Ok, whatever.  When you get right down to it, they are both great cars for different reasons.  Fiero handles great in terms of it being a small, light and tossable car.  The Mustang's mission in life is to go fast and it does that well.  V6's Head to head?  Pre 99 Stang's are real close to Fiero's in acceleration and it would almost always boil down to the talent of the driver IMO. 99+ 'Stangs are a little faster... not by much and a skilled Fiero driver can still pull out a victory in a race.  If the 'Stang driver is good, he's probably gonna win. ||||reg||1
